<title>JAPAN: TOSHIBA LOWERS 1997/98 GLOBAL PC SALES TARGET.</title>
<headline>TOSHIBA LOWERS 1997/98 GLOBAL PC SALES TARGET.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toshiba Corp said on Monday that it had revised downward its global sales target for personal computers to one trillion yen from 1.1 trillion yen for the year to March 31, 1998.</p>
<p>Slower-than-expected sales of notebook PCs in the United States prompted the revision, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>Toshiba at present has no plans to cut its PC prices to reflect lower prices for Intel Corp's microprocessors, he said.</p>
<p>Japan's top PC maker NEC Corp has not made any changes to its 1997/98 sales target, although sales in the April-June quarter were slightly below expectations, an NEC spokesman said.</p>
</text>
